{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for every n ≥ 3 the set of node sets -1 ≤ x₁ < … < xₙ ≤ 1 with minimal Lebesgue constant is uncountable (Rack and Vajda 2015, Theorem 2.5). The proof shows that a minimiser exists (continuity, compactness and blow-up of the Lebesgue constant as nodes collide), rescales it to a canonical minimiser, and shrinks it slightly.",
